  "title": "Europe experiences record-breaking heatwaves and droughts as global ocean temperatures rise",
  "summary": "Central and western Europe is expected to experience more intense heatwaves as high pressure systems bring warm air from southern Europe, with forecasts showing temperatures reaching up to the high 30s Celsius for France, Spain, Italy, and Germany. The heatwave has led to record-breaking temperatures in several European countries, including Slovakia and Austria, and has caused widespread evacuations and challenges in agriculture and water resources. Europe's oceans recorded their hottest July on record, partly fueled by developing El Niño conditions, while drought and wildfires intensify across the continent.",
